[h1]Phobos Agriculture[/h1]
[h2]Solar-system economy in 0.10.0[/h2]
Cultivation, cooking, irrigation and nutrient-workup machinery, planting stock, nutrients, root-water charges, cartridges, makeup and pipes gain bounded offers at 15 additional placed vanilla retail markets. Food-producing centres receive higher authored availability. Makeup receives the industrial category; terminal biomass/rejects receive trash. Recorded intermediates retain their separate meaning. Base values, cohorts and fluid records are preserved.
Requires Phobos Framework 0.23.0 or newer. Authored availability follows native economic roles; native supply/demand, merchant terms and restocking remain in control. No new settlements, guaranteed stock or live-price promises. Prepared offline, not gameplay-validated or published.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/solar-system-economy.md]Regional coverage, sources and limits[/url]
[h2]Optional completion cues in 0.8.0[/h2]
Requires Phobos Framework 0.22.0 or newer. After starting a meal or crop, optionally watch its completion once through local controls, C1 or F3. A quiet tone means the meal was delivered or the whole cohort became harvest-ready; it never harvests automatically. Shared volume/mute, no replay after loading and no growth-stage or irrigation pings. Gameplay/listening review pending.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/shared-completion-cues.md]Supported events, shared controls and original audio provenance[/url]
[b]Version:[/b] 0.12.1
[b]Publication status:[/b] Not published - development candidate

Grow potatoes and lettuce and cook portions aboard your ship using Phobos' Verdemorrow Firstlight-4 Cultivation Racks and Hearth-2 Galley Cookers.

[h2]Current features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Choose a separate lettuce seed-production cycle, with flowering/seed-head art and finite seed harvests. Food lettuce remains a separate crop.
[*]New treatment jobs use finite cartridge capacity by drainage mass and return unused medium; older queued jobs keep their original contract.
[*]W2 and conduit repair bills reflect their equipment roles.
[*]Visible crop stages track the saved crop cohort in the four-tray rack.
[*]Twelve distinct original item sprites identify planting stock, supplies, food and retained waste.
[*]Find planting stock and food in eligible native fridge loot, and seeds, nutrients, water charges, treatment cartridges and loose pipes in locked-crate/bulk-cargo loot. Chances are configurable and existing loot remains intact.
[*]Crew load finite supplies, plant, harvest and maintain equipment; automatic controls support the growing environment.
[*]Use finite manual water and nutrients, or an optional Groundwork W2 supply unit and placed irrigation conduits.
[*]Mix crop-specific nutrient solution in the W2 and deliver water and nutrients through the same supported circuit.
[*]Buy or construct equipment through ordinary acquisition routes, with repair, dismantling and retained waste.
[*]INSTALL catalogue: Firstlight-4, Hearth-2 and W2 under APPS; irrigation conduit under MISC. Intact and damaged forms retain normal physical installation requirements. Prepared; gameplay review pending.
[/list]

[h2]Limits and save behaviour[/h2]
[list]
[*]The prepared package includes the native data directory required for the game to recognize Agriculture.
[*]Experimental candidate; the complete growing/cooking loop still needs in-game evaluation.
[*]Loot additions apply only to future native generation; existing containers are not refilled. Not every fridge uses the eligible pool. No large machinery or generated process waste is added.
[*]Four trays represent one crop cohort, not four independent crops or four times the yield.
[*]One W2 can explicitly serve up to eight paired racks. Receiving and pumping require explicit controls and pause after reload.
[*]Short growth cycles, crop budgets, nutrient mixtures and simplified chemistry are authored gameplay choices, not research results.
[*]Recorded drainage supports finite cartridge-powered treatment with retained rejects; legacy process solution remains waste. There is no perfect nutrient recycling or unlimited water.
[/list]

[h2]Requirements and installation[/h2]
Ostranauts 1.0.1.5, BepInEx 5 and Phobos Framework 0.25.0 or newer. Shipbreaker C1 access is optional. The Ship's Water adapter is scoped to inspected version 0.16.1; manual supply remains available.

This is a maintained pre-publication page draft, not a download announcement. No Workshop item has been published for this draft. Use the installation guide for source/prepared-package availability and loader setup. Do not remove required providers from saves that contain their content.

