[h2]Fluid network update[/h2]
One W2 can explicitly supply up to eight compatible racks using one shared pump budget. Irrigation routes retain finite parcels and apply authored resistance and transit delays; broken routes keep their contents.

[h2]Equipment and item reference[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/agriculture-item-reference.md]Read this mod’s item reference[/url] for functions, use, acquisition and applicable base prices, repair and salvage. Generated tables follow the current source candidate; proposals and prototype limitations are labelled.

[h2]Nutrient recovery research[/h2]
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/agriculture-nutrient-recovery.md]Read the researched nutrient-recovery and workup direction[/url]. That research now supports the implemented 0.9.0 crop-residue chain and wet-reject capture described below. Wastewater nutrients remain uncharacterized; recorded-drainage treatment stays separate.

[h2]Nutrient recovery and optional wet-reject collection[/h2]
[b]Prepared, not yet gameplay-validated.[/b] Agriculture 0.9.0 adds the Groundwork B2 bench, recorded crop recovery and equal-mass makeup formulation. Select a physical nutrient charge in W2 for gradual consumption during blending; consumables cannot be repaired or restored. Old crop residue remains uncharacterized. Framework 0.22.0 and Shipbreaker 0.20.0 support measured wet-reject capture from [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3757331189]Valtora’s Ship’s Water 0.16.1[/url]. Full or unavailable linked collectors hold wastewater in its source tank. No wastewater-to-fertilizer recipe is claimed. [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/agriculture-nutrient-production.md]Operating guide, economic limits and research attribution[/url].

[h2]Recycler controls and collector placement[/h2]
Requires Framework 0.24.2 for shared panel feedback. Other Agriculture machinery hides its portrait slot if artwork is unavailable; errors and distinct action notices remain visible.
Agriculture 0.11.1 corrects repeated control-panel status and the empty Recycler portrait square. With Shipbreaker 0.24.1, the C2 collector may stand on bare structural floor directly against a full two-tile Recycler edge, including its front. Keep the opposite service side clear for pedestrians. Saved links and cargo remain intact; misaligned pairs wait for correction or Unlink. Prepared offline; gameplay confirmation pending.

[h2]Bulk merchant stock[/h2]
Increase successful local and regional offers to wholesale lots for machinery, irrigation conduit and consumables, including W2/B2, seeds, nutrients, water charges, treatment cartridges and makeup. Uses Framework 0.24.0; prices, rare fridge/crate loot and existing inventories are unchanged.
Normal restocking is required; updating does not refill existing shops. [url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/merchant-stock.md]Current quantities and restocking guide[/url]. Prepared candidate; in-game stock/capacity review pending.

[h2]Dosing and workup save correction[/h2]
Agriculture 0.12.1 fixes protected-state faults when no dosing charge is selected, a workup bench is idle or a recovery job needs no supplement. Exact input identities and paid energy are preserved; unknown or corrupt records remain blocked. Restart and reload after updating. Automated save-wrapper checks are not gameplay validation.

[h2]Crew standing orders[/h2]
Added standing work for selected crop cohorts, finite replenishment, harvest/replant, potato cooking, nutrient workup, configured water routes, recorded drainage recovery and approved storage. Added Agriculture and Cooking training, novice eligibility and qualified-worker preference. Crop growth, chemistry and material yields are unchanged. Preserved source seed stock and configured crew-water reserves. Clearing unwanted living crops and draining usable solutions require separate permission. Added routine resume-after-load selection and supported onboard time-skip accounting through Framework 0.25.0.
Requires Framework 0.25.0. Ship’s Water and Shipbreaker remain optional. No new recipe for uncharacterized wet rejects; no gameplay validation or Steam publication.
[url=https://github.com/phobos-dthorga/phobos-ostranauts/blob/main/docs/crew-automation.md]Crew controls, time-skip limits and owner checks[/url]. Optional native-task coexistence with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3789049955]LOGUSS’s Common Sense modules[/url]; added study preserves [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3788237703]jossla’s Study at Terminals[/url].
